    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d393">

                <pb facs="0883" n="852" xml:id="pg852"/>

                <head>393. Memorandum From the President’s Assistant for National Security Affairs
                    (Kissinger) to Secretary of State Rogers<anchor n="1" xml:id="d393-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1972-07-29">July 29, 1972</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>War Powers Legislation</item>
                </list>
                <p>The President has considered various approaches to the War Powers legislation now
                    under consideration in the Congress and has decided that Congressman Clement
                    Zablocki should be informed that any compromise on this legislation that
                    includes a specification of the President’s war powers or a time limitation on
                    their exercise would be unacceptable. Would you please arrange to have
                    Congressman Zablocki so informed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">Henry A. Kissinger</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
